# What does NOT upload to the EAS build workers.
#
# .easignore REPLACES .gitignore for the upload — it is not additive. The
# docs are explicit: "If you create a .easignore file, the EAS CLI
# prioritizes it over the .gitignore file", and instruct copying every
# .gitignore entry in. A file holding only the two directories below would
# therefore have STARTED uploading node_modules, dist — and .env, which
# holds secrets. So everything above the marker is a faithful mirror of
# .gitignore; keep the two in sync when either changes.
#
# FINGERPRINT: this file is an easBuild hash source (@expo/fingerprint
# sourcer/Expo.js hashes ['eas.json', '.easignore']), which is exactly how a
# two-line eas.json edit orphaned build 12. It is therefore listed in
# .fingerprintignore alongside eas.json — same reasoning: it shapes what
# UPLOADS, never what compiles into the binary. Verified fingerprint-neutral
# against both build 19 runtimes (d84c8ac3 Android, 6a9f0dba iOS) under
# `eas env:exec production` on 2026-08-21.

# ---- mirror of .gitignore ------------------------------------------------

# dependencies
node_modules/

# Expo
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
expo-env.d.ts

# Native
.kotlin/
*.orig.*
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision

# Metro
.metro-health-check*

# debug
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*

# macOS
.DS_Store
*.pem

# local env files
.env
.env*.local
server/.env

# supabase local dev
supabase/.temp

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo

# generated native folders
/ios
/android

# loose marketing/reference files at repo root (not app assets)
/*.mp4
/*.jpg
/Snapt_Claude_Code_Handoff_Documentpdf
/Snapt -  App - REAL/
.claude/settings.local.json

# ---- build-upload-only exclusions (the reason this file exists) ----------
# 161MB of local design references and logo masters that no build step
# reads. They were riding to the build workers on every single build.
/Images/
/Logo/
